     "<div style=\"direction:ltr\">Hey, </div><div style=\"direction:ltr\">i wrote a little bit of code in JS to spice up my app to allow navigating between H1 tags using the keyboard. </div><div style=\"direction:ltr\">pretty simple stuff : </div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><br></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&lt;script type=&quot;text/javascript&quot;&gt;</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>// scroll between headers </font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>i = -1</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>tag = &quot;H1&quot;</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>document.onkeypress=function(e){</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> var e = window.event || e</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> var x = document.getElementsByTagName(tag)</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> var s = String.fromCharCode(e.charCode)</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> if (s == &#39;j&#39;)  {</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>   i += 1</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>   if (i &gt; x.length) i = 0 </font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> } else if (s == &#39;k&#39;) {</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>   i -= 1</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>   if (i == 0) i = x.length</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> }</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> // alert(i + &quot; &quot; + x[i]. innerHTML)</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span> x[i].scrollIntoView()</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>}</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">&lt;/script&gt;</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><br></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\">i add this script to my shiny app like this ... </div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">## ui.r</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">shinyUI(</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  bootstrapPage(</font></div><div style=\"direction:ltr\"><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">  includeHTML(&quot;keyboard_scroller.js&quot;) , </font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">....</font></div><div><br></div><div>and i have a lot of <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">headerpanel </font>objects in the page. </div><div><br></div><div>when i load the app the scrolling is not smooth. sometimes it worked and sometimes it doesn&#39;t. </div><div>it could work for two <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">H1</font> tags and then i need to scroll around with the mouse to make it work again. </div><div>when testing the script on a simple HTML page it worked smoothly. </div><div>i would appreciate any help. </div><div><br></div><div>Haki.</div></div></div>"
